{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): morning. i've done his obs. blood pressure one thirty two over eighty four, pulse seventy six, sats ninety eight percent. he was halfway back to the car.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): lovely, thank you. come on through, both of you. what's brought you in?",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (PATIENT): honestly, nothing. she's blown it up. it's just a bit of backache.",
  "[SEG0004] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): he says nothing. then he can't sit through dinner.",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (DOCTOR): alright. tell me where it is, and how long it's been bothering you.",
  "[SEG0006] person_3 (PATIENT): lower back. um, a couple of weeks. well, actually, three weeks.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (DOCTOR): does it stay in the back, or does it go somewhere?",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (PATIENT): shoots down the right leg. only when i've sat too long. hardly anything.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (DOCTOR): and how is the pain when you're walking?",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (PATIENT): work's been mad, that's the thing. err, dave at the depot said do cat stretches. did them twice. pointless.",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (DOCTOR): mm. dave in a minute. when you walk, though, is it better or worse?",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (PATIENT): walking's fine. sitting's the annoying bit. still not a big deal.",
  "[SEG0013] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): he drives for the council. in the van half the day.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (DOCTOR): any numbness in the leg? pins and needles?",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (PATIENT): no.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (DOCTOR): and weakness? does the foot drag or give way?",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (PATIENT): not that either.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (DOCTOR): any change in the waterworks, or the bowels?",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (PATIENT): never. all fine.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (DOCTOR): fever, or feeling properly unwell alongside it?",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (PATIENT): not really. i'm alright.",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (DOCTOR): what are you using for the pain at the moment?",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (PATIENT): ibuprofin, two hundred milligrams three times a day. uh, no, the four hundred ones, twice a day. i've got asthma too, not that it matters, salbutamol blue inhaler, two puffs if i need it.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (DOCTOR): got it. we'll keep the ibuprofen as it is, with some food. hop on the couch and i'll lift each leg, just say when it pulls.",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (DOCTOR): straight leg raise on the right pulls at about forty degrees. the left goes all the way, no problem. power in both feet is normal and there's no foot drop.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): coming back to the asthma, any wheeze at the moment?",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (PATIENT): no... well, sometimes, if i've been rushing for the van.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): and a cough at night?",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (PATIENT): not that either.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): right. to my mind this is mechanical low back pain with a touch of nerve irritation. nothing today that looks sinister.",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (DOCTOR): i'd like the nurse to take bloods thursday morning, a full blood count and a crp, to check for inflammation. no need to fast. come before ten and take your tablets as usual.",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (NURSE): thursday morning, before ten. i'll book that.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (DOCTOR): if those come back borderline we'll add an esr. i'll book physio, they've a slot next tuesday. i'll see you here in two weeks. if it hasn't settled by then we'll arrange a scan, but not yet.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (DOCTOR): in the meantime keep moving. don't take to your bed.",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (PATIENT): yeah alright. it'll have gone by then, you'll see."
 ],
